What ran out is the **assertion timeout**, which is separate from the overall test timeout. Auto-retrying assertions like `toHaveText()` have a default timeout of 5 seconds. Your error log confirms this: "expect.toHaveText with timeout 5000ms".

Bumping the timeout is a supported way to handle this, but whether it is the "right" response depends on your situation. You can increase the timeout for a specific assertion by passing a timeout option, or configure it globally in your `playwright.config.ts`:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  expect: {
    timeout: 10_000,
  },
});
```

The documentation notes that auto-retrying assertions will re-fetch the element and check it repeatedly until the condition is met or the assertion timeout is reached. If your button is visible in a screenshot but the assertion receives an empty string, it suggests the element was fetched while it was still in an intermediate state (e.g., rendered but not yet populated with text) and the assertion timeout expired before the text became available.

