To record videos only when a test fails, set the `video` option to `'retain-on-failure'` in your Playwright configuration file. This setting records video for every test but removes the files for those that pass.

In your `playwright.config.ts` file, configure it within the `use` object:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  use: {
    video: 'retain-on-failure',
  },
});
```

The resulting video files will be saved in your test output directory, which is typically `test-results`.

