llm_response:
To organize your tests into a "Smoke" set and a "Default" set with the specified retry behavior, you should use projects in your `playwright.config.ts` file. This allows you to define specific filters and retry counts for each group.

Add the following to your `playwright.config.ts`:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  projects: [
    {
      name: 'Smoke',
      testMatch: /.*smoke.spec.ts/, // Adjust the regex to match your smoke test files
      retries: 0,
    },
    {
      name: 'Default',
      testIgnore: /.*smoke.spec.ts/, // Excludes the smoke tests from this project
      retries: 2,
    },
  ],
});
```

By defining these projects, the "Smoke" project will run only the tests matching the `testMatch` pattern with zero retries, while the "Default" project will run all other tests (excluding those matched by `testIgnore`) with two retries.

