llm_response:
To skip a test only on Firefox, you can use `test.skip` with a condition inside the test body:

```javascript
test('your test name', async ({ page, browserName }) => {
  test.skip(browserName === 'firefox', 'Still working on it');
  // ... rest of your test
});
```

If you want to skip an entire group of tests or all tests in a file for Firefox, you can use a callback:

```javascript
test.skip(({ browserName }) => browserName === 'firefox', 'Still working on it');

test('test 1', async ({ page }) => {
  // ...
});
```

Playwright will run the test but abort it immediately after the `test.skip` call when the condition is met.

